{"id": "EUVD-2026-103685", "enisaUuid": "800a57be-49e6-3192-80c2-0bebfa2873e6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't let memory failures leak blocks and kill repairs\n\nLOLLM complains that a memory allocation failure in\nxrep_newbt_add_blocks results in online repair leaking blocks that were\npreviously allocated to write a new btree, but the problem is worse than\nthat -- a limitation of the codebase is that the callers cannot undo the\ntransaction /and/ return the error -- either you undo all changes and\ncommit the transaction, or you error out and the filesystem goes down.\n\nHowever, the new btree space reservation object isn't that big (~48\nbytes).  Let's just do a NOFAIL allocation and the problem goes away.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:14:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3380151cf0ce8ad0c1d356fed51e4b69e1d28e50", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b15c79fca28060fd9c7e77f2c3ebc4ba023974e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e0d3372a84029da1768c7a4c4601484af5b58a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab1c416d2377cdc16123ef521aac4da1c468c3d4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vx8f-phpg-5qwp", "CVE-2026-98445"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2dddfb6d-0ad6-3b9a-815a-116848d691b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2e9bf0a6-120d-3262-b32f-089facf20873", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be408417630427984a1fddd069f30b245793234c <3380151cf0ce8ad0c1d356fed51e4b69e1d28e50"}, {"id": "3e3b8548-80d2-3586-bbc6-78d08dc8a2a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "4fc766e0-9f7a-3673-a17a-488d756bbd3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "5ca131fe-9671-3f4d-b41d-2877a6cb5c88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be408417630427984a1fddd069f30b245793234c <b15c79fca28060fd9c7e77f2c3ebc4ba023974e8"}, {"id": "7351fdc9-81fa-3304-86f3-2e3550dc9a4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be408417630427984a1fddd069f30b245793234c <ab1c416d2377cdc16123ef521aac4da1c468c3d4"}, {"id": "757b2765-6d99-3acb-a912-12e19ede0de6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "9dd4323f-f170-3234-996e-f8743f3db166", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be408417630427984a1fddd069f30b245793234c <0e0d3372a84029da1768c7a4c4601484af5b58a2"}, {"id": "bd683819-b98d-36c7-a53e-46fee48c3b46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f56b3f2d-ba66-3626-a542-be54851de1ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7ac6f896-d0d9-3399-ae7f-fa6413eb3e05", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}